    "findings": [
      "All 81 fixed scope paths match their exact frozen SHA-256; the accepted root content receipts and corrected canonical configuration are within that immutable scope.",
      "Own I–IV global power values are .05/.075/.10/.125 and child duration is 7 seconds; this is consistent with the general Superiority entry and distinct from the melee-qualified sibling. Effective cap is three, with the internal placeholder/offset not presented as a fourth player-visible stack.",
      "The kill helper uses died plus elite OR special; the held-slot gate and absence of event-source-item equality are stated accurately. Attack resolution precedes event handling and cache refresh, so a kill does not retroactively strengthen its own attack.",
      "Seven-second refresh/one-stack decay, timer continuation while unwielded, return before decay, and parent removal on item removal are accurately distinguished.",
      "Crowbar BASE_ACTIONS aliases, push-follow versus pure push, sticky hits and dodge-exit attack=0/impact behavior are described separately. Force Sword M1/M2 special-active sticky routes and M3 active-cleave distinction are retained; fling damage_type is not confused with ranged attack_type.",
      "RAW text and same-hash locale pairing are preserved; formatter values, percentage-point versus relative increase, power-level formula, and limits on final HP damage are stated consistently in the checked examples and source review.",
      "No unresolved contradiction or material scope gap found; RAW omissions on held/source-item/cache/action-route details are not mislabeled as errata."
    ],
